            <h2>Airlines Flying from Salt Lake City to New York</h2>
            <p>Five carriers operate nonstop or connecting service between Salt Lake City and the New York area: Delta Air Lines, JetBlue Airways, United Airlines, American Airlines, and Southwest Airlines.</p>
            <h3>Delta Air Lines</h3>
            <p>Delta dominates this route from its Salt Lake City hub, offering the most comprehensive schedule and seamless connections.</p>
            <p><b>Highlights:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Multiple daily nonstops to JFK, LaGuardia, and Newark on Airbus A220, A321neo, and Boeing 737 aircraft</li>
                <li>SkyMiles earning with Medallion elite benefits and complimentary upgrades</li>
                <li>Free Wi-Fi for SkyMiles members on equipped aircraft</li>
                <li>Delta Sky Club access at SLC Terminal A and JFK Terminal 4 for eligible passengers</li>
                <li>Industry-leading operational reliability and on-time performance on this corridor</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>JetBlue Airways</h3>
            <p>JetBlue brings its value-driven, customer-friendly model to this transcontinental route with competitive fares and generous legroom.</p>
            <p><b>Highlights:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Daily nonstop red-eye service to JFK aboard Airbus A220-300 aircraft</li>
                <li>The most legroom in coach among domestic carriers - up to 32 inches of seat pitch</li>
                <li>Free high-speed Wi-Fi, live TV, and complimentary snacks and soft drinks</li>
                <li>TrueBlue points earning with no blackout dates and family pooling</li>
                <li>Mint business-class recliners on select rotations for premium comfort</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>United Airlines</h3>
            <p>United connects Salt Lake City to its Newark hub with mainline service and extensive onward international connections.</p>
            <p><b>Advantages:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Daily nonstops to Newark Liberty International on Boeing 737 and Airbus A320 family aircraft</li>
                <li>MileagePlus earning with Premier qualifying credits toward elite status</li>
                <li>Economy Plus extra legroom and Polaris business-class lie-flat seats on select widebody rotations</li>
                <li>United Club access at Newark Terminal C for members and eligible passengers</li>
                <li>Star Alliance connectivity for travelers continuing to Europe, Asia, and beyond</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>American Airlines</h3>
            <p>American links Salt Lake City to New York through its Dallas/Fort Worth hub and seasonal direct service, backed by the world's largest loyalty program.</p>
            <p><b>Benefits:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Connecting service to JFK, LaGuardia, and Newark via Dallas/Fort Worth and Charlotte</li>
                <li>AAdvantage mileage earning with Loyalty Points toward elite status</li>
                <li>Main Cabin Extra legroom and Flagship business-class on transcontinental rotations</li>
                <li>Admirals Club access at DFW and JFK Terminal 8 for eligible passengers</li>
                <li>Extensive domestic and international feed enabling complex itineraries on a single ticket</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Southwest Airlines (Low-Cost)</h3>
            <p>Southwest brings its no-frills, flexible model to the route with service into LaGuardia, the closest airport to Manhattan.</p>
            <p><b>Features:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Multiple daily nonstops between SLC and LaGuardia aboard Boeing 737 aircraft</li>
                <li>Rapid Rewards points with no blackout dates and fully refundable flexibility.</li>
                <li>Two free checked bags on every fare - a rarity in modern air travel</li>
                <li>No change fees; pay only the fare difference if plans shift</li>
                <li>Easy positioning for Manhattan, Queens, and Long Island destinations</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Connecting Options</h3>
            <p>One-stop itineraries route through Denver, Dallas/Fort Worth, Chicago, Charlotte, Phoenix, and Atlanta, often priced below nonstops. Frontier Airlines offers ultra-low-cost connecting service through Denver for budget-conscious travelers.</p>
            <h2>Seasonal Variations</h2>
            <h3>Peak Season: Mid-November through January, June through August</h3>
            <p>The route's two high seasons combine holiday travel with summer tourism and business conferences.</p>
            <p><b>During peak months:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Airfares reach annual highs, with Thanksgiving week and Christmas commanding the steepest premiums</li>
                <li>New Year's Eve in Times Square and the summer theater season draw massive leisure demand</li>
                <li>Hotel rates in Manhattan climb with minimum-stay requirements; Broadway tickets and restaurant reservations book out weeks ahead.</li>
                <li>July and August bring peak humidity and heat, but also free outdoor concerts, Shakespeare in the Park, and rooftop cinema seasons.</li>
                <li>College move-in weekends in late August create secondary fare spikes</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Shoulder Season: Mid-February through May, September through Early November</h3>
            <p>The sweet spot for value, weather, and manageable crowds.</p>
            <p><b>Advantages:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Economy fares typically run 20 to 35 percent below peak levels</li>
                <li>Spring cherry blossoms in Central Park and fall foliage in the Hudson Valley</li>
                <li>Fashion Week in February and September, plus the New York Film Festival in autumn</li>
                <li>Comfortable walking weather with crisp autumn air or mild spring breezes</li>
                <li>Better upgrade availability and award seat inventory across all carriers</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Off-Peak Value Windows: Late January through Early February, Early December</h3>
            <p>Post-holiday weeks deliver the cheapest fares of the year.</p>
            <p><b>Benefits:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>January is historically the cheapest month, with round trips averaging near $272</li>
                <li>Uncrowded museums, shorter lines at the Statue of Liberty, and easier Broadway ticket access</li>
                <li>Winter restaurant week deals and post-holiday retail sales</li>
            </ul>
            <p><b>Considerations:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>January temperatures in New York average in the low 30s°F; lake-effect winds can feel biting</li>
                <li>Snowstorms can disrupt Northeast operations; travel insurance is advisable</li>
                <li>Some outdoor attractions operate reduced winter hours</li>
            </ul>
